​ The Mechanism of Recycling
In this "rolling cosmology," the universe operates as a self-repairing recycling plant. As galaxies age and their worldline bundles tighten, they eventually undergo gravitational collapse into black holes.

Black Hole Dropout: Rather than disappearing into a mathematical singularity, the mass of a black hole "drops out" from the 3D resolving surface (Σ 

