The Continuous Crash: These streamers eventually "crash into" the singular origin point. This implies that the Big Bang is constantly "exploding" as massive objects from across the 4D manifold cycle back into the initial state.

​ Baryogenesis and Particle Origin
This persistent explosion serves as a supplemental mechanism for creating matter.

Topological Saturation: Because the 4D manifold has finite bending energy, black holes cannot merge into infinite density; instead, they collapse into their tightest stable configurations—double- or triple-braided worldlines—which are perceived in 3D as mesons and hadrons.

Eschatological End-State: Massive celestial bodies effectively "unwind" back into fundamental particles, satisfying the Topological Saturation Limit (Q≤3).

​ Misinterpreted Energy
The framework speculates that the energy generated by this continuous internal "action in the block" is what standard physics misinterprets as Dark Energy. This suggests that the accelerating expansion of the 3D timesheet is driven by the internal pressure of black hole matter recycling into the singular origin deep within the 4D bulk.

​ Dimensional Asymmetry
The theory asks if space-time asymmetry is a local phenomenon. While we perceive the fourth dimension moving relative to the first three, deep in the block, different dimensions may move relative to one another, potentially "opening up" or unfolding in complex ways as the universe evolves.

